<title>INDIA: Standard Chartered cuts Indian prime rate.</title>
<headline>Standard Chartered cuts Indian prime rate.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard Chartered Bank said on Saturday it had cut its Indian prime lending rate to 17.0 percent per annum from 18.0 percent, effective November 4.</p>
<p>The maximum spread over the prime rate would be 4.0 percent, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The cut follows similar reductions by most other banks after the central bank's monetary policy statement on October 19 which boosted liquidity.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
